  "description": "TIJLOQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C210 H196 Ho8 N24 O44 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),2(C1 H4 O1),12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho7 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho8 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.615-4.120 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.72-121.38°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C212H228Cl4Ho8N24O74. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
